Description: restore the use_v4l2_codec_rpi GN option dropped by RPi-Distro
 RPi-Distro's own rpi/0009-Build-add-use_v4l2_codec_rpi-gn-option.patch
 (originally by John Cox) defined BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI), which our
 local-hevc/000{1,4,7} patches gate Pi-specific code behind. That upstream
 patch is present in the vendored 147.0.7727.116 debian/ tree
 (vendor/rpi-distro-chromium/debian/patches/rpi/0009-...) but is no longer
 in RPi-Distro's 151.0.7922.173 debian/patches/series at all -- it was
 silently dropped somewhere in RPi-Distro's own rebase, not something we
 changed. Without it, `BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI)` fails to compile with
 "function-like macro 'BUILDFLAG_INTERNAL_USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI' is not
 defined" in media/gpu/chromeos/video_decoder_pipeline.cc and the v4l2
 delegate .ccs. Re-adding it here (verbatim content, new location in our
 series) restores the flag; default is true here (matching upstream's
 default) since debian/rules doesn't set use_v4l2_codec_rpi explicitly and
 our whole build only targets Pi hardware anyway.
Author: chromium-rpi-hevc (originally John Cox <jc@kynesim.co.uk>, RPi-Distro)
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/media/gpu/BUILD.gn
+++ b/media/gpu/BUILD.gn
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ buildflag_header("buildflags") {
     "USE_VAAPI=$use_vaapi",
     "USE_VAAPI_IMAGE_CODECS=$use_vaapi_image_codecs",
     "USE_V4L2_CODEC=$use_v4l2_codec",
+    "USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI=$use_v4l2_codec_rpi",
     "USE_LIBV4L2=$use_v4lplugin",
     "USE_LINUX_VIDEO_ACCELERATION=$use_linux_video_acceleration",
   ]
--- a/media/gpu/args.gni
+++ b/media/gpu/args.gni
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ declare_args() {
   # platforms which have v4l2 hardware encoder / decoder.
   use_v4l2_codec = false
 
+  # Indicates if this is V4L2 on RPi.  Only compiles stateful V4L2 code
+  # and removes all legacy codecs
+  use_v4l2_codec_rpi = true
+
   # Indicates if VA-API-based hardware acceleration is to be used.
   use_vaapi =
       is_linux && !is_castos &&
